---
# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  DEFERRED — THIS IS THE ENFORCEMENT FLIP. DO NOT ENABLE IT CASUALLY.      ║
# ║                                                                          ║
# ║  WP11 stage 4. Written, reviewed and committed, but deliberately NOT      ║
# ║  delivered to the cluster. Enabling it requires a human who has already   ║
# ║  completed stages 2 and 3 and can say yes to every line of the checklist  ║
# ║  in README.md. Getting locked out of your own IdP is not a situation an   ║
# ║  agent can recover from.                                                  ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE CANNOT REACH THE CLUSTER AS IT STANDS ──────────────────────
# Two independent gates are closed, and BOTH must be opened by hand:
#
#   1. The filename ends in `.DEFERRED`. ArgoCD's directory source only reads
#      *.yaml, *.yml and *.json, so this file is invisible to GitOps. Renaming
#      it to end in `.yaml` opens gate 1.
#   2. Even then, the ConfigMap would sit unused in the namespace. The
#      authentik chart only mounts ConfigMaps named in `blueprints.configMaps`
#      in ../../values.yaml. Adding `authentik-blueprint-mfa-required-admins`
#      to that list opens gate 2.
#
# Two gates, not one, because a single accidental rename must not be able to
# lock the only administrator out of every admin surface on the platform.
#
# ── WHAT IT DOES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# It binds `platform-admin-mfa-validation` (defined in
# 20-mfa-enrollment-optional.yaml) into the authentication flow at order 25 —
# after identification at order 10, before the inert original at order 30 — and
# gates it on membership of the `platform-admins` group. It then attaches the
# same group check, NEGATED, to the existing order-30 binding, so exactly one
# of the two validation stages ever runs and nobody is challenged twice:
#
#     platform-admins member   → order 25 runs (enrol-or-challenge), 30 removed
#     everyone else            → order 25 removed, order 30 runs (skip, as now)
#
# ── THE DETAIL THAT DECIDES WHETHER THIS WORKS AT ALL ────────────────────────
# `evaluate_on_plan: false` together with `re_evaluate_policies: true` is not
# stylistic. It is verified in authentik 2026.5.6:
#
#   FlowPlanner._build_plan() only evaluates a binding's policies at plan time
#   when evaluate_on_plan is true. At plan time nobody has identified yet, so
#   `pending_user` is unset, the group check runs against AnonymousUser,
#   returns False, and the stage is dropped from the plan. MFA would appear
#   configured and never once challenge anyone.
#
#   With evaluate_on_plan false and re_evaluate_policies true, the binding gets
#   a ReevaluateMarker, and ReevaluateMarker.process() builds
#   PolicyEngine(binding, plan.context.get(PLAN_CONTEXT_PENDING_USER, ...)) —
#   i.e. the identified user. The group check then means what it reads as.
#
# If you change either flag, you are choosing between "MFA enforced" and "MFA
# silently inert", and the two look identical from the login page.
#
# ── A GROUP BINDING, NOT AN EXPRESSION POLICY ────────────────────────────────
# PolicyBinding.passes() short-circuits: `if self.group: return
# PolicyResult(self.group.is_member(request.user))`. No Python expression, no
# AnonymousUser attribute access, nothing to get subtly wrong. The repo's
# existing `policy-admins-only` expression policy is the right tool for
# Applications, where the user is already authenticated; it is the wrong tool
# here.
#
# ── ROLLBACK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rename this file back to `.DEFERRED` and remove the ConfigMap from
# `blueprints.configMaps`, then let ArgoCD sync. Blueprint entries are not
# reverted by deleting the blueprint, so ALSO delete the two policy bindings
# and the order-25 flow-stage binding in the Authentik admin UI (Flows →
# default-authentication-flow → Stage Bindings). If you cannot reach the admin
# UI because of the change you are rolling back, that is precisely what
# docs/BREAK-GLASS.md is for — use the break-glass account, which is not in
# `platform-admins` and therefore never traverses order 25.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: authentik-blueprint-mfa-required-admins
  namespace: authentik
  annotations:
    argocd.argoproj.io/sync-options: ServerSideApply=true
data:
  mfa-required-admins.yaml: |
    version: 1
    metadata:
      name: InfraWeaver MFA Required — platform-admins
      labels:
        blueprints.goauthentik.io/description: >-
          Binds the platform-admin MFA validation stage into the
          authentication flow for members of platform-admins only, and
          suppresses the inert default stage for those same members.
    entries:
      # ── 1. The stage binding at order 25 ──────────────────────────────────
      - model: authentik_flows.flowstagebinding
        state: present
        id: binding-platform-admin-mfa
        identifiers:
          target: !Find [authentik_flows.flow, [slug, default-authentication-flow]]
          order: 25
        attrs:
          target: !Find [authentik_flows.flow, [slug, default-authentication-flow]]
          stage: !Find [authentik_flows.stage, [name, platform-admin-mfa-validation]]
          order: 25
          # Read the header before touching these two lines.
          evaluate_on_plan: false
          re_evaluate_policies: true
          policy_engine_mode: any
          invalid_response_action: retry

      # ── 2. Only platform-admins reach it ──────────────────────────────────
      - model: authentik_policies.policybinding
        state: present
        identifiers:
          target: !KeyOf binding-platform-admin-mfa
          order: 0
        attrs:
          target: !KeyOf binding-platform-admin-mfa
          group: !Find [authentik_core.group, [name, platform-admins]]
          enabled: true
          order: 0
          negate: false
          timeout: 30
          failure_result: false

      # ── 3. …and only they SKIP the original inert stage ───────────────────
      # `!Find` on authentik_policies.policybindingmodel (not on
      # flowstagebinding) is deliberate: a policy binding's target is a
      # pbm_uuid, while FlowStageBinding's primary key is a different column
      # (fsb_uuid). Targeting the flowstagebinding directly would resolve to
      # the wrong UUID and the binding would silently attach to nothing.
      # Verified live: both resolve paths were compared and only this one
      # returns the binding's pbm_uuid.
      - model: authentik_policies.policybinding
        state: present
        identifiers:
          target: !Find [authentik_policies.policybindingmodel, [flowstagebinding__stage__name, default-authentication-mfa-validation]]
          order: 0
        attrs:
          target: !Find [authentik_policies.policybindingmodel, [flowstagebinding__stage__name, default-authentication-mfa-validation]]
          group: !Find [authentik_core.group, [name, platform-admins]]
          enabled: true
          order: 0
          negate: true
          timeout: 30
          failure_result: false
